---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
  title="Get a Reddit API key | threadshot"
  description="How to create a Reddit app and copy its client ID for threadshot."
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl px-4 py-10 md:py-16 lg:px-8">
    <h1
      class="font-display text-4xl leading-[1.02] font-extrabold tracking-[-0.02em] sm:text-5xl"
    >
      Get a Reddit API key
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-5 text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink-2">
      threadshot reads posts through an app on your own Reddit account. All it
      needs from you is that app's client ID.
    </p>

    <ol class="mt-8 list-decimal space-y-3 pl-5 marker:font-semibold">
      <li>
        Sign in to Reddit, then open{" "}
        <a
          class="link"
          href="https://www.reddit.com/prefs/apps"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          target="_blank">reddit.com/prefs/apps</a
        >.
      </li>
      <li>
        Click <strong>are you a developer? create an app...</strong> (or{" "}
        <strong>create another app...</strong> if you already have one).
      </li>
      <li>Give it any name, such as threadshot.</li>
      <li>
        Choose <strong>installed app</strong>. It has no secret, which is all
        threadshot needs.
      </li>
      <li>
        Enter <code class="rounded-ui bg-canvas px-1">http://localhost</code> as
        the redirect URI. Reddit's form asks for one and threadshot never uses
        it.
      </li>
      <li>
        Click <strong>create app</strong>. Your client ID is the short string
        shown under the app's name. Copy it.
      </li>
      <li>
        <a class="link" href="/">Go back to threadshot</a> and paste it into
        the Client ID field.
      </li>
    </ol>

    <h2
      class="mt-12 font-display text-2xl font-extrabold tracking-[-0.02em]"
    >
      Which app type?
    </h2>
    <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5">
      <li>
        <strong>Installed app:</strong> cannot keep a secret, so it has none.
        Pick this one.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Script:</strong> runs on hardware you control and has a secret.
        Paste the secret into threadshot's optional Client secret field. It only
        has access to your own account.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Web app:</strong> meant for a service on a server you control.
        You don't need it here.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2
      class="mt-12 font-display text-2xl font-extrabold tracking-[-0.02em]"
    >
      Can't create an app?
    </h2>
    <p class="mt-3">
      Reddit asks builders to read its Responsible Builder Policy first and may
      need to approve access before it lets you create an app. If you can't get
      a key, <a class="link" href="/#bookmark">use the bookmark instead</a>. It
      reads a post from the Reddit page you already have open, so it needs no
      key.
    </p>

    <h2
      class="mt-12 font-display text-2xl font-extrabold tracking-[-0.02em]"
    >
      Reddit's documentation
    </h2>
    <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5">
      <li>
        <a
          class="link"
          href="https://github.com/reddit-archive/reddit/wiki/OAuth2"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          target="_blank">Reddit OAuth2 documentation</a
        >: app types, client IDs and the installed-app login.
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          class="link"
          href="https://support.reddithelp.com/hc/en-us/articles/42728983564564-Responsible-Builder-Policy"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          target="_blank">Responsible Builder Policy</a
        >: the rules for creating an app and using the API.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</Base>
